From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_wed: unbind the WLAN driver before the
 Ethernet driver

The WED instances belong to the Ethernet driver: mtk_wed_exit() frees
them when the Ethernet driver is unbound.  A WLAN driver attached to one
keeps a pointer to it in its struct mtk_wed_device, along with the rings
and buffers it set up through it, and uses them until it detaches.
Unbinding the Ethernet driver while a WLAN driver is attached therefore
leads to a use-after-free.

Link the WLAN device to the Ethernet device when the WLAN driver
attaches, so that the driver core unbinds the WLAN driver first.  The
link goes away when the WLAN driver is unbound.

Fixes: b3d0d98179d6 ("net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: fix possible memory leak in mtk_probe()")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
@@ -2870,6 +2870,20 @@ mtk_wed_attach(struct mtk_wed_device *de
 		? &dev->wlan.pci_dev->dev
 		: &dev->wlan.platform_dev->dev;
 
+	/* The WED instances belong to the Ethernet driver, which frees them
+	 * when it is unbound: have the driver core unbind the WLAN driver
+	 * first.  The link goes away with the WLAN driver.
+	 */
+	if (!device_link_add(device, hw->eth->dev,
+			     DL_FLAG_AUTOREMOVE_CONSUMER)) {
+		dev_err(device, "failed to link to %s\n",
+			dev_name(hw->eth->dev));
+		hw->wed_dev = NULL;
+		module_put(THIS_MODULE);
+		ret = -ENODEV;
+		goto unlock;
+	}
+
 	dev->hw = hw;
 	dev->dev = hw->dev;
 	dev->irq = hw->irq;
